{number: 64}
{title: Only Trust Him}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Come, every soul by sin oppressed,
There's mercy with the [G7] Lord,
And [C] He will surely give you rest
By [G7] trusting in His [C] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Only trust Him, only trust Him,
Only trust Him [G7] now;
He [C] will save you, He will save you,
He will [G7] save you [C] now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
For [C] Jesus shed His precious blood
Rich blessings to be-[G7] stow;
Plunge [C] now into the crimson flood
That [G7] washes white as [C] snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Yes, [C] Jesus is the Truth, the Way,
That leads you into [G7] rest;
Be-[C] lieve in Him without delay,
And [G7] you are fully [C] blest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Come [C] then, and join this holy band,
And on to glory [G7] go,
To [C] dwell in that celestial land,
Where [G7] joys immortal [C] flow.
{end_of_verse}
